{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/450354-grasping-the-nuances-of-resources-4","id":450354,"title":"Grasping the nuances of Resources 4+","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-20T06:18:49-07:00","id":450354,"title":"Grasping the nuances of Resources 4+","content":"I'm trying to grasp the difference between Resources 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9.<br /> I've always heard that 5 in a trait is the best a human can ever accomplish in one lifetime. But the likes of Bill Gates, Steve Jobs and the rest of the top guys/gals in Forbes list of Billionaires cannot possible be the top of Resources 5 right? The condition of Resources 6 is to be part of and be able to influence national/international economics and that definetly sounds like for example Bill Gates.<br /> <br /> So, can you people give real life and /or fictional (Movies, Series) examples of various levels of Resources?<br /> For example, how much would the main character from Wolf of Wallstreet have in Resources?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T07:36:01-07:00","id":450420,"title":"","content":"Bill Gates currently has Resources 5, However I'd say that Google as a company has Resources in 7-8 Range. The only group in the WoD that might have Resources 10 is probably the Syndicate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T08:59:06-07:00","id":450495,"title":"","content":"5 asa maximum does not apply to backgrounds. of course you can have a lot of contacts or alies.<br /> <br /> depending on exactly what amount resources 10 correspond 2 there may be other groups that have it or are close to it. clan giovanni for instance. or maybe pentex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T10:27:24-07:00","id":450574,"title":"","content":"As mark said, the five-dot limit representing peak human accomplishment really only applies to Attributes and Abilities, not so much for Backgrounds.<br /> <br /> As for your question, the difference lies between <i>rich</i> and <i>wealthy</i>. For example: A star NBA player is rich. The guy that signs <i>the players</i> checks is wealthy. For more concrete, real-world examples, Bill Gates easily had a score of 6 at the height of his influence, while Steve Jobs had a 4, but <i>Apple Computers</i> had (and has) a 6 or so.<br /> <br /> Starting about Resources 5, one worries less about paying their internet bill and more about buying state legislatures to incentivize for their corporations.<br /> <br /> Also, 10 isn't necessarily the limit. Depending upon how one feels about conspiracy theories, something like the Bilderberg Group could have a score of 20, 30, or even 100.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T11:09:09-07:00","id":450637,"title":"","content":"I personally don't really bother with the 6+ background stuff.<br /> <br /> When you're looking at what the books that get into 6+ in a background is defined as, I think it is far better handled horizontally (that is spreading out into new backgrounds) than vertically (making Resources go higher). Bill Gates is certainly highly influential because of his money. But also because he's got lots of dots in Fame, Status, Allies, Contacts, Influence, and so on. To me, that's what separates the super-rich people you hear about and see doing things in the world, compared to the ones that you only know about if you look up the lists of the current super-rich.<br /> <br /> Oddly mirroring the Arch-Spheres debates in Mage, if I were to delving into what Backgrounds over 5 look like, I'd rather break out Adventure! (sure not a WOD game, but still a ST system one) where there's simply one level above 5 that represents stepping it up to a degree where scale stops really being an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T12:43:39-07:00","id":450717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/450354-grasping-the-nuances-of-resources-4?p=450574#post450574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As mark said, the five-dot limit representing peak human accomplishment really only applies to Attributes and Abilities, not so much for Backgrounds.<br /> <br /> As for your question, the difference lies between <i>rich</i> and <i>wealthy</i>. For example: A star NBA player is rich. The guy that signs <i>the players</i> checks is wealthy. For more concrete, real-world examples, Bill Gates easily had a score of 6 at the height of his influence, while Steve Jobs had a 4, but <i>Apple Computers</i> had (and has) a 6 or so.<br /> <br /> Starting about Resources 5, one worries less about paying their internet bill and more about buying state legislatures to incentivize for their corporations.<br /> <br /> Also, 10 isn't necessarily the limit. Depending upon how one feels about conspiracy theories, something like the Bilderberg Group could have a score of 20, 30, or even 100.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> didn't steve jobs have a net worth of around 10 billion? if you ask me that's around resources 8.<br /> i think bill gates highest net worth was 130 bllion. that's propably a 9.<br /> <br /> after all resources 4 is(inflation excluded) 500.000. 5 is 5 million. so logically 6 should be 50 million.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:06:26-07:00","id":451061,"title":"","content":"Do bear in mind that Resources values were defined in the early 90s. If they were written from scratch for today, they wouldn't look the same. And the 130 Billion for Gates was when he was still a majority holder of Microsoft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T19:48:12-07:00","id":451199,"title":"","content":"Net worth is not income, and the Resources background is basically telling you how much &quot;fun money&quot; you can spend each month without worrying about your normal expenses. $30,000 per month is usually far more than anyone needs to ever spend at one time during the game. What's the point of boosting Resources to represent anything beyond that? It becomes like Spinal Tap, &quot;But this one goes to 11&quot;. The purpose of Resources is so the ST can quickly decide &quot;Yes, you can afford that&quot; and not that he needs to be an accountant. If an ST is going to deny someone with Resources 5 to buy something, it's probably for other reasons than that he decided it actually cost $30,000.01.<br /> <br /> The purpose of these rules is not meant to simulate the real world. It's to provide just enough mechanics so that most things likely to come up in game can be covered. When you try to define everything that has ever happened in the real world, the game mechanics just break down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/450354-grasping-the-nuances-of-resources-4?p=450637#post450637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you're looking at what the books that get into 6+ in a background is defined as, I think it is far better handled horizontally (that is spreading out into new backgrounds) than vertically (making Resources go higher). Bill Gates is certainly highly influential because of his money. But also because he's got lots of dots in Fame, Status, Allies, Contacts, Influence, and so on. To me, that's what separates the super-rich people you hear about and see doing things in the world, compared to the ones that you only know about if you look up the lists of the current super-rich.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Heavy Arms that to simulate a character with even more wealth, it is probably better to expand more Backgrounds than just Resources. At Resources 5, you have everything you should need for <u>cash flow</u>. Past that, what you really want are the things that wealth &quot;buys&quot; with it - Influence, Allies, Contacts, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T16:32:00-07:00","id":453337,"title":"","content":"I know that in the games I was playing in back in the mid 90s, we defined Resources 6 as the point at which someone became a billionaire. There were only about 350 people in the world with that kind of money at the time, and it was just before the dotcom boom that started boosting individual fortunes into the tens of billions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}